<article class="env-lemma" id="0FWF">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0FWF">Lemma <span data-tag="0FWF">10.49.3</span>.</a> Let $k$ be a field. Let $S$ be a $k$-algebra. The following are equivalent </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
$S$ is geometrically integral over $k$, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
for every finite extension $k'/k$ of fields the ring $S \otimes _ k k'$ is a domain, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$S \otimes _ k \overline{k}$ is a domain where $\overline{k}$ is the algebraic closure of $k$. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Follows from Lemmas <a href="/tag/05DY" data-tag="05DY">10.49.2</a>, <a href="/tag/030V" data-tag="030V">10.44.4</a>, and <a href="/tag/037K" data-tag="037K">10.47.3</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>